    "summary": "Long pebble, of igneous rock, modified and carved with two crests, the main one being in the form of a fish such as a sturgeon, with a large head, prominent round eyes, dorsal fins carved in formline, ribs and vertebrae, the tail with a human face with lips pursed round for singing; at the other end is the head of a sea mammal, perhaps a seal or sea lion, neatly carved with formline features, the back of the head delineated by the end of the fish tail. Possibly used as an amulet or wand.",
